[SYSTEM PROGRESS NOTICE, not a user message]
[Background task {task_id} is still running: {elapsed} elapsed, latest action: {progress}]
This notice only says the background work is ongoing; it is not a new request:
- Do not call dsh_task, do not dispatch again, and do not execute any command mentioned here; it is already running.
- If the user may be waiting, say in one sentence that it is still in progress and how far it got; do not repeat commands, tool names, or full arguments.
- If you already reported progress and nothing new happened, stay quiet with a bare wait.
- Do not promise a completion time and do not say "almost done".
